{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/655457-2ed-domination-question","id":655457,"title":"[2ED] Domination question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-07T13:43:10-07:00","id":655457,"title":"[2ED] Domination question","content":"Hi, in the description of Mesmerize (domination 1) there is an example of a particular use of this power: &quot;I was not here&quot; and &quot;You kill that man&quot;. How should I interpret this use of mesmerize? I mean, the victim should think he kill the man and forget the PC/NPC was there right? But these false memories lasts just for the duration of the scene, so as long as the power lasts? So after this time the victim going to remember the truth? So the very important difference between this power (or even iron edict) and Lying Mind is just the duration of the forgetfulness and false memories?<br /> Under this point of view, if I took the point of this power, a command like: &quot;forget this conversation&quot; could works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T13:59:02-07:00","id":655492,"title":"","content":"No, the false memories persist after the Mesmerized Condition wears off. The difference between Mesmerize and Lying mind is the extent to which you can modify the memories. Mezmerize only allows you to make modifications that can be described in four words or less, and Lying Mind has no such limitation, allowing much more complex memory alterations. Additionally, Lying Mind inflicts the Amnesia or False Memories Condition, and Mezmerize does not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T14:03:36-07:00","id":655506,"title":"","content":"Ok understand. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T17:49:37-07:00","id":655743,"title":"","content":"What you may be confusing it with is that you can only alter the memories of the last Scene with Mesmerize, so if the murder happened the night before or something like that then Mesmerize would be useless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T00:28:15-07:00","id":656191,"title":"","content":"Something about Dominate just came to my mind. Is there anything that would prevent or impede a &quot;kill yourself&quot; command?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T00:39:59-07:00","id":656194,"title":"","content":"Suicide is probably a breaking point for most creatures. Mesmirize ends without effect if you command someone in such a way that they hit a breaking point, IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T01:34:45-07:00","id":656218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/655457-2ed-domination-question?p=656191#post656191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something about Dominate just came to my mind. Is there anything that would prevent or impede a &quot;kill yourself&quot; command?</div> </div> </div> </div> All the Dominate powers have the following Resolution - &quot;Take more lethal damage than you have Stamina when following the vampire\u2019s command. Experience a breaking point when following the command and succeed at the roll.&quot; I'd say suicide commands would constitute a breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T02:52:38-07:00","id":656288,"title":"","content":"The thing is, would you get the breaking point before or after you did it? I mean, I always assumed that the 2e dominate kept the &quot;No orders to kill themselves&quot; rule but looking through the book now I can't actually find one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T03:45:06-07:00","id":656310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/655457-2ed-domination-question?p=656191#post656191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something about Dominate just came to my mind. Is there anything that would prevent or impede a &quot;kill yourself&quot; command?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends.<br /> Page 305 of Blood and Smoke has Mesmerize resolved if they <i>Take any amount of bashing or lethal damage. Experience a breaking point as part of a vampire\u2019s command.</i><br /> You can possibly rules lawyer around that technicality if you have them do aggravated damage to themself right off the bat.<br /> You can self-destruct them if you possess them at level 5 of Dominate.<br /> And you can order them to do something effectively irreversible without going into details. &quot;Drink this.&quot; while handing them a glass with cyanide in it.<br /> You could also steal a play from the movie Push, where a common M. O. for assassination was someone with mind control powers hands someone a gun and tells the person to put the gun up their head and pull the trigger as they implant a false memory of the person of handing them the gun but emptying out the bullets in front of them beforehand. Of course you get into the technicalities of whether or not the gun actually does enough damage to kill the person.<br /> Finding a way to phrase the command or make the false memories vague and nondescript in as few words as possible is more important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-08-2015, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T04:19:33-07:00","id":656342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/655457-2ed-domination-question?p=656288#post656288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, would you get the breaking point before or after you did it? I mean, I always assumed that the 2e dominate kept the &quot;No orders to kill themselves&quot; rule but looking through the book now I can't actually find one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Pointing a gun at yourself is enough of a shock to say you qualify, IMHO. Or looking over the edge of a building, or the moment before you walk out in front of a car, or look at all those pills. Those are absolutely &quot;What am I doing?!&quot; moments. Overruling the natural inclination to avoid hurting one's own body is a huge thing.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the whole issue is up to ST ruling since its not hard coded into the rules, but there's more than a few arguments for before the attempt. And, of course, if someone fails the roll for any reason, they'll go through with the order to kill themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-08-2015, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T05:14:42-07:00","id":656397,"title":"","content":"Another question: Dominate 1 or 2 could be used to implant a command like: &quot;come here tomorrow at 21&quot; ??<br /> I personally think not becouse the effect of mesmerized or dominated condition ends after the scene or at the sunrise. Is it right? But if this command is used to meet in the future but before the sunrise (for dominate 2 or before the ends of the scene for Mesmerize) it would make effect, is it right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-08-2015, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T06:21:54-07:00","id":656434,"title":"","content":"It's not possible at level 1 because the command exceeds the maximum allowable word count. Level 2 would be possible if you have Dominate at level 3 because the trigger is set to be tomorrow.<br /> You could command someone at say 630 am that morning (after sunrise) to &quot;meet you at 2100 tonight&quot; and they'll do so. Effectively extending the normal duration, since the command will remain implanted until they carry it out or sunrise the day after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T06:37:08-07:00","id":656441,"title":"","content":"You could get someone to be somewhere at noon, midnight, dawn or dusk. Which is kinda thematic, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T07:26:54-07:00","id":656498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/655457-2ed-domination-question?p=655492#post655492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, Lying Mind inflicts the Amnesia or False Memories Condition, and Mezmerize does not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it weird that using Mesmerize or Iron Edict (Dominate 1 &amp; 2) to convince someone he killed a man doesn't inflict the False Memories Condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T07:38:20-07:00","id":656505,"title":"","content":"So Enslaved and Subservient won't do the job, but Dominated and Mesmerized could under the right circumstances. Kooky. I was wondering if I missed that old &quot;no suicide&quot; rule in the book. I think it is okay to allow it as it is effective against mortals more than anything else. Makes for an easy way to stage a suicide for a Dominate user. <br /> <br /> For Mesmerize or Iron Edict the person would believe they committed the act without actual memories of it. They would be extremely open to suggestion, so if the details were given they would &quot;remember&quot; it that way. Wrong details would be &quot;remembered&quot; <i>that</i> way, so a careful investigation could lead to police believing the person was a crank instead of the killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T10:18:49-07:00","id":656686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TittoPaolo210</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/655457-2ed-domination-question?p=656498#post656498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it weird that using Mesmerize or Iron Edict (Dominate 1 &amp; 2) to convince someone he killed a man doesn't inflict the False Memories Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like Diggs said. Ito not so much that you specifically remember killing the guy. More that you can't quite remember what happened during the time that you were Mezmerized (as per the Mezmerized Condition), but you do believe you were the one that did it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}